---
import site from '../data/site.json';
const steps = [
  'Fold the cup, for example into a C shape, and insert it.',
  'To close, pull the strings at the stem steadily; pull only until the petals close, not so hard that the cup comes out.',
  'Remove the closed cup by the stem.',
  'Empty it with a syringe through the opening.',
  'Reset the Flower mechanism by pushing the tail back until the petals reopen.',
  'Clean: wipe off residue, then immerse and shake in 70 % isopropanol.',
];
---
<section id="use">
  <h2>Use and cleaning of the Flower designs</h2>
  <p class="lead">
    The handling steps below apply to the two Flower designs (Flower Low,
    flown, and Flower High), whose pull strings close the petals; the other
    mechanisms are operated differently and were not taken this far. The
    SpaceCup is a research prototype, not a certified medical device, and is
    not intended for personal use.
  </p>
  <ol class="steps">{steps.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ol>
  <p>
    The cleaning study covered Flower Low, Flower High, Drawstring and
    Twister, plus a reference cup. Of the three cleaning methods tested,
    70 % isopropanol with shaking left the fewest colonies. The narrow gaps
    between the Flower’s strings held residue that steam reached poorly.
    Results are under <a href="#validation">Validation</a>; the procedure is
    in <a href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/docs/use.md`}>docs/use.md</a>.
  </p>
</section>
<style>
  .steps { padding-left: 22px; display: grid; gap: 8px; margin: 20px 0; }
  .steps li { color: var(--fg-dim); }
  .steps li::marker { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: var(--mono); }
</style>
